Push notifications with Firebase in iOS

Firebase Cloud Messaging

Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) is a cross-platform messaging solution that lets you reliably send messages at no cost.



1.	Configure Apple dev account
Enable the Push notifications service.
Create APNS certificate with the app’s App ID.
Install the SSL certificate in keychain and export the .p12 file.

2.	Configure Firebase account
Register for firebase account and create a new project. 
In project settings, add firebase to iOS/Android app.
Add the bundle identifier and  download the plist file to drop in the project.
Install pod into firebase project. 
In firebase portal, select cloud messaging and upload the APNS .p12 file for development and production.

 

